 (tells MF runtime to use\n  dynamic import() for the ESM remote entry)\n- Add docs/BUNDLER-COMPARISON.md documenting the limitation and\n  migration recommendations","tree":{"sha":"fb1e681f29a51f62bc8800c9e52a6d9ca8216b2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/craigmorrison/example-module-federation/git/trees/fb1e681f29a51f62bc8800c9e52a6d9ca8216b2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/craigmorrison/example-module-federation/git/commits/0f39a3f3163895125b2cef0f83aca5519569c839","verification":{"payload":"tree fb1e681f29a51f62bc8800c9e52a6d9ca8216b2d\nparent f64351a7f682368b935dbbb3bba24e150d13361e\nauthor Craig Morrison <public@craigmorrison.co.uk> 1774825967 +0100\ncommitter Craig Morrison <public@craigmorrison.co.uk> 1774825967 +0100\n\nfix: vite producer uses build+preview for cross-bundler dev compat\n\nVite''s dev server serves ESM with HMR preamble which is incompatible\nwith webpack/rspack consumers that load remote entries as classic\n<script> tags. The workaround is to build the production bundle and\nserve it via vite preview.\n\n- app-people-list dev script now runs: tsc && vite build && vite preview\n- Consumer points to mf-manifest.json (tells MF runtime to use\n  dynamic import() for the ESM remote entry)\n- Add docs/BUNDLER-COMPARISON.md documenting the limitation and\n  migration recommendations\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQQT651tqtkFuxKe0FZz2ZytI9oKDQUCacmx7xsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQc9mcrSPaCg29FwD/apvhARYkDxd7afKcsupv\nox2T5MWBiggp2jTCyHEICfQA/jS6iQG6ZphaSXgqIIccL6SuXdVl1xswTubZ5BPW\nJTwF\n=N740\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-29T23:12:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/868089?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigmorrison/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigmorrison/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigmorrison/following{/other_user